<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Trips</span>
<h1>Hanoi to Soc Son by Motorbike: Route Planning | Hanoi Motorbike Guide</h1>
<p>Route planning for Soc Son is the art of leaving the city without fighting it, because the district sits to the north where the capital thins into delta countryside and the airport corridor carries the traffic the quiet roads do not want. The plan is a spine and a set of ribs rather than a turn-by-turn, a chosen way out, a chosen corridor and a willingness to let the district&rsquo;s lanes write their own small sentences. This guide plans the whole shape without inventing a single kilometer, minute or closure, and explains why that refusal is the plan&rsquo;s strongest feature.</p>
<p>The machines, the briefing and the honest numbers come from Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, Hanoi, open daily 09:00 to 21:00, where the desk briefs every rider heading north. Begin at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/">Hanoi motorbike trips</a> hub, absorb the parent <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/long-distance-motorbike-trip-planning/">long-distance motorbike trip planning</a> guide, see the machines and terms on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> page, review the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a> for riding and safety, and keep <a href="/renting-a-motorbike-in-vietnam/">renting a motorbike in Vietnam</a> open for the legal layer.</p>
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#sec-1">The Shape Of The Way North</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-2">A Philosophy Instead Of A Turn-By-Turn</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-3">Leaving The Fringe Honestly</a></li>
